.el .ds Aq '
.TH tensor-wasm-bench 1  "tensor-wasm-bench "
.SH NAME
tensor\-wasm\-bench \- Benchmark local invocation latency (P50/P95/P99/max)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtensor\-wasm bench\fR [\fB\-\-export\fR=\fIEXPORT\fR] [\fB\-\-n\fR=\fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-tenant\fR=\fITENANT\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIFILE\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Loads a \fB.wasm\fR file, spawns a fresh instance per iteration, invokes the named export, records the wall\-clock duration, and prints a table with P50/P95/P99 and max latencies. The bench measures end\-to\-end \fBspawn + call + terminate\fR so it captures cold\-start cost as well.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-export\fR=\fIEXPORT\fR [default: main]
Name of the export to call on each iteration.
.TP
\fB\-\-n\fR=\fIN\fR [default: 100]
Number of iterations to run. Must be at least 1.
.TP
\fB\-\-tenant\fR=\fITENANT\fR [default: 0]
Tenant id (currently unused by the local bench path; retained for parity with HTTP\-shaped subcommands).
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIFILE\fR]
Path to the \fB.wasm\fR file to benchmark.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
tensor\-wasm bench tests/wasm\-fixtures/vector_add.wasm \-\-export add \-\-n 1000
.fi
.RE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
tensor\-wasm(1), tensor\-wasm\-run(1)
